PART 3: GENERAL BASE THEOREM
  For ANY integer b with gcd(b,p) = 1:
  b^{C(p,2)} ≡ (b/p) (mod p²)

  Proof: b^{C(p,2)} = (b^{(p-1)/2})^p ≡ (b/p)^p = (b/p) mod p²
  (since (b/p) = ±1 and (±1)^p = ±1 for odd p)
